  "note": "PASS by the preregistered rule: none of the 7 fixed pairs is WORSE_BOTH (2 DOMINATES: sesame lamp -> tallow candle, incandescent -> CFL; 5 TRADE_OFF). Four of the five trade-offs entered with less energy but more hours of work per lumen-hour (whale oil, town gas, Edison vs kerosene x3.33 labor, Edison vs gas x2.30); the fifth, kerosene at Silliman 1855, entered with 1.57 times MORE device energy than the sperm-oil lamp but 0.014 times the labor, so an energy-only rule would have picked the loser. Successor families later dominated the incumbent's row: gas by 1855, kerosene by 1880, electric by 1900; whale oil never dominated the 1830 tallow candle in this table. Device energy basis only: Edison 1883 is better in both only if the plant efficiency exceeds eta* = 0.061 (vs kerosene) and 0.095 (vs gas); plant efficiency is not in the dataset, so this is not decided. Not blind (SEEN_FULL); not UET-distinct (standard economics expects the same). L2 approved by the author on 2026-11-18."
